  partName: Right Rear Bolt
  description: The Right Rear Bolt is a tiny, complex-shaped component located at
    the bottom-right-rear of the engine, made of Material.001, responsible for securing
    the engine's rear section, ensuring its stability and preventing potential damage
    from stress and vibrations, and its complex shape enables a secure fit with adjacent
    parts. The bolt's rear position requires it to withstand the engine's exhaust
    system temperatures and pressures, making material selection critical. The Right
    Rear Bolt works in conjunction with other bolts to maintain the engine's structural
    integrity, highlighting the importance of proper bolt torque and maintenance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
